 quite a bit smaller so  they decided to put larger speaker  enclosures  to fill the gaps now fast forward to  2020 and we now have a new teardown from  owc  that reveals similar internals but a  whole lot of extra room  now that they've gone away with the  physical hard drive  and just watch what happens when they  remove the speaker enclosures  most of the outdated imac case is still  being unused  now before i dig deep into the rest of  those internals  and what i believe is going to happen to  them on the apple silicon models  i want to switch over to what the new  design will look like on the exterior  way back in 2011 apple released the  27-inch  thunderbolt display to replace the apple  cinema display  then on october 20th of 2012 just  over a year later apple introduced the  fully redesigned imac  with an identical display with the same  aspect ratio  and the same resolution it looked almost  identical  except that the imac had a chin on the  bottom and then the 21.5 inch model  was basically the same except scaled  down now this brings us to june 3rd  2019 when apple revealed the pro display  xdr  that went on sale in december from the  front the rounded corners and black  bezels  look very similar to an ipad pro with  flat edges on the side  as well and when you're looking from the  side the pro display xtr  is quite a bit thick and that's because  the casing has the passive cooling vents  that are milled out of a solid block of  aluminum to match the mac pro's design  that adds extra thickness and it's a  high-end  multi-layer display that outputs a ton  of light  for hdr editing now if you've been  following the 24-inch imac redesigned  rumors  there were many leaks pointing to apple  redesigning the imac  with an ipad pro like design which is  basically what the pro display xdr  already looks like the only problem is  that the pro display xtr is a bit bulky  having thick sides and a large bulky  stand so here's what i think the  redesigned imac is gonna look like  and how apple is gonna achieve it on the  front side it'll look  just like the pro display xdr with the  same thin bezels  except that it'll have a chin on the  bottom with a small apple logo  why the chin well because the imac has  always had the chin it needs to have  the chin if the 2012 27 inch imac  didn't have a chin it would literally be  identical to the thunderbolt display  when looking at it from the front apple  needs to make sure  that when you see an imac you know it's  an imac and we do  because it's always had a chin and the  same thing goes for the redesigned apple  silicon imac  it's gonna have a chin with an apple  logo except that i think the chin is  gonna be a little bit smaller  but by how much i don't know but it'll  probably be smaller than the massive  chin  we currently have the sides of the imac  are going to be flat  just like the pro display xdr except  that i believe  the sides are actually going to be a bit  thinner now the  interesting part is that i think the  newly redesigned imac  is gonna have a totally flat back no  more hump like we have currently  on the imac it'll be flat just like the  pro display xdr  except that it won't have the same  cheese grater vents  now you might be asking how is apple  gonna fit the guts or the internals of  the imac  with it being thinner than the pro  display xdr and  not having a hump well first off the  hump design is not gonna work  with thick flat edges because that's  exactly how the 2011 imac look like  and apple won't be going back to that  design apple wants their new imac to  look modern  for a new modern apple silicon chip and  a new modern macos design and if you  think about it  all three of those things come from the  ipad pro  which looks modern with its flat sides  already has a modern apple silicon chip  and as you already know mac os big sur  looks a whole lot like ipad os 14.  so apple is going all in with the new  rounded corner  and flat edge look which is exactly what  the iphone 12 is gonna look like  as well the ipad air 4 is also rumored  to be taking on the same design  as the current ipad pro this makes sense  for apple to do because this transition  is a massive one  and by the time it's finished all of  apple's flagship devices  are going to look very similar design  wise now getting back to how apple can  fit all of those internals in a flat  and thin imac this brings us to that  teardown of the 2020 imac  from owc this right here is the guts of  the current 27-inch imac  which is now smaller this year because  the hard drive is now gone  since it comes with an ssd at the base  price  it's absolutely tiny compared to the  size of the imac  now of course this is the 27 inch model  but this logic board  without the hard drive is also now  pretty small in the 21 and a half inch  model as well  now here is that same imac with the  power supply removed  it becomes even smaller now once it  takes out the main board and flips it  over  we see the reason for the hump on the  imac there are two  quite large heat sinks one for the cpu  and one for the graphics chip  and along with that we have the user  upgradable ram  that sticks out quite a bit so it makes  sense why apple used this design  in the 2012 imac and now let's finally  get into the design of the apple silicon  imac  and how it can easily have thin sides  and a completely flat back  if you've watched some of my videos on  the apple silicon chips  you'll know that they're designed to run  very efficiently  using much less power than intel chips  and you'll also know that apple is  ditching the amd  gpu and going with their own custom  apple gpu  which will be integrated into the main  soc so let's take a look at that logic  board again  on the apple silicon max there obviously  won't be  a hard drive which is already missing on  the current imac  with apple silicon that huge power  supply on the left side  is going away since the graphics will be  integrated into the main soc  we no longer need all of that space for  that chip on the right side  or its massively thick heatsink and  since apple silicon is going to be more  efficient  the socketed intel cpu and its thick  heatsink  is going away it'll likely have a much  thinner cooling design  like on the 16-inch macbook pro and the  large fan  no longer needs to be that large anymore  they can make it thinner  and more spread out thanks to all that  extra space  the user-replaceable ram that is also  quite a bit thick is most likely going  away which is a bit sad  but it makes sense for an apple silicon  chip which integrates everything  into one soc now if you think about it  everything is going to be soldered onto  the main board  the apple silicon chip the ram the  storage  and the power supply will be built in  the cooling system will be much smaller  than before since there's no need  for a dedicated graphics ship that takes  a huge amount of power  and the apple silicon chip itself takes  much less power than an intel cpu  basically the main board is going to be  much thinner than before  and all of the leftover empty space can  be filled up by the speaker enclosures  which will be thinner and more spread  out so it totally makes sense for the  guts of the imac to fit into a chassis  that's thinner than the pro display xdr  and finally  i think the stand is going to look very  similar to the one on that display  which is already shaped like an ipad pro  except that the stand will obviously be  included for the same price and  permanently attached to the back  like on the current imac so there you  guys have it that's my speculation for  the redesigned imac  it'll look just like the pro display xdr  with the same rounded corners  the same thin bezels except with a chin  that's likely going to be smaller than  the current one the sides will be flat  and it'll be thinner overall with a flat  back the 24 inch imac will get it first  probably within the next seven months  and then the larger imac will likely get  the redesign  in the second half of next year if you  agree with my speculation on the  redesign  let me know down in the comment section  below and be sure to check out our apple  product merch like our arm  apple silicon t-shirt or our mask down  in the merch shelf below  and if you can't wait to see this new  imac redesign click the circle above to  subscribe  for more videos like this one thanks for  watching and we'll see you in the next  [Music]  one
 

